course: dictionary
lesson: 13775
title: Working out intimately
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intimately means in a very close way. When you know something intimately, you know it very well, often because you have spent a long time with it. «Mia knew the old forest intimately, every path and every stream.» Mia had walked there for years, so she knew it very well.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The two villages are intimately linked by the river.» Linked tells you the villages are connected, so intimately means very closely connected. Try the swap check: put «very closely» in place of intimately, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Careful: intimately can also mean close and personal, like between family or best friends. «The sisters talked intimately about their secret hopes.» Here it shows they shared private feelings. The meaning changes with the subject, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Intimately is an adverb, so it tells you how something is known or done.
fact: «Intimately» means in a very close, detailed way, or very well from long experience.
fact: «Intimately» can also mean in a very close and personal way, as between close family or best friends.
fact: «Intimately connected» means two things are so closely linked that one affects the other.
fact: In a science text you might read, «the plants are intimately connected to the soil».
exercise: «Mia knew the old forest intimately.» What does intimately mean here? | Only for one day | *Very well, from long experience | Very far away | Very quickly and without care
exercise: «The two villages are intimately linked by the river.» What does intimately suggest? | *Very closely connected | Angry with each other | Lost and confused | Quite cold
exercise: «The sisters talked intimately about their secret hopes.» Find and copy one word that tells you the talk was private. | their | *secret | talked | sisters
test: «The doctor knew her patients intimately, and remembered each one's name and story.» What does intimately mean here? | Very late | *Very well, from long experience | Very quickly | Very angrily
test: Ben says «intimately» is just a fancy word for «near». Why is he wrong? | It means quietly | It means exactly near, so he is right | It means far away | *It means very closely or very well, not just nearby
exam: Which sentence uses intimately to mean very closely connected? | The bus was late this morning | We ate pizza for lunch | *The brain and the body are intimately linked | The cat slept on the mat
